1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,660
This is my uncle's story. In
1982 E.C. (1989/90), he was a

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:07,210
sailor in the Ethiopian Navy.

3
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:11,720
The work was heavy. Sleep was
four hours, at most.

4
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:16,490
But on Thursday, the ship would
sail to Massawa. To him, Massawa

5
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:19,480
was like heaven.

6
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:24,450
On Tuesday, while working inside
the ship, his foot slipped.

7
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:28,380
His ankle twisted. His arm
broke.

8
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:32,860
His commander, who loved him
like a son, told him: "You stay

9
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:35,210
here. Rest."

10
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:39,700
His heart broke. He lost all
hope; it felt like the end of

11
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:41,890
the world.

12
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:46,660
On Thursday morning, the ship
left without him.

13
00:00:49,810 --> 00:00:53,500
That same Thursday, an attack by
Eritrean fighters sank the ship.

14
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,490
His comrades and his commander
stayed with the sea.

15
00:00:58,090 --> 00:01:00,530
On Friday, he heard the news. He
calls it the day he was born

16
00:01:00,530 --> 00:01:03,260
again.

17
00:01:05,090 --> 00:01:06,620
The fall that broke him that day
was the hand that saved his

18
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:08,440
life.

19
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:15,140
Today he preaches the gospel. He
tells everyone one thing: "Let

20
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:18,490
God lead your life."
